BT /F2 16 Tf 54 723 Td (Atlas Month-End Close Support Runbook) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 701 Td (Document ID: it-atlas-month-end-close-runbook) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 679 Td (Owner: IT Business Applications \(Atlas team lead Aoife Gallagher\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 657 Td (Last reviewed: 2025-05-12) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 635 Td (Applies to: Atlas ERP production) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 610 Td (1. Purpose and scope) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 588 Td (This runbook describes how IT Business Applications supports Group Finance during the monthly) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 575 Td (close of the Atlas ERP system. It covers the technical preparation before the close window) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 562 Td (opens, the controlled release of the month-end batch jobs, the payroll export to our external) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 549 Td (payroll bureau, the period lock, and the tidy-up activities once Finance has signed off. It is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 536 Td (written for the Atlas support engineer on duty for the close and for the Beacon service desk) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 523 Td (analysts who triage Finance tickets during the window.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 501 Td (The runbook applies to the Atlas production environment only. The Atlas test and pre-production) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 488 Td (environments do not run the month-end batch chain on a schedule; if Finance asks for a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 475 Td (rehearsal close in pre-production, raise a separate Beacon request and follow the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 462 Td (pre-production notes held by the Atlas team.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 440 Td (Month-end close is the single most business-critical recurring event for Atlas. The period) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 427 Td (close drives statutory reporting for the four legal entities, intercompany settlement, and the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 414 Td (monthly payroll for UK staff. Year-end close \(March, because the Meridian fiscal year starts on) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 401 Td (1 April\) follows the same procedure with the additional year-end steps owned by Group Finance;) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 388 Td (those steps are outside the scope of this document.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 363 Td (2. Overview of the close window) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 341 Td (The close window runs from BD-2 through BD+3, where BD means business day relative to the last) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 328 Td (calendar day of the month. BD-1 is the last business day of the month and BD+1 is the first) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 315 Td (business day of the new month. Business days follow the UK \(Leeds\) calendar, because Group) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 302 Td (Finance is based in Leeds; local holidays in Rotterdam, Austin or Penang do not move the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 289 Td (window.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 267 Td (A change freeze applies for the whole close window in accordance with the Change Management) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 254 Td (Procedure v2 \(it-change-management-procedure-v2\). During the freeze no normal or standard) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 241 Td (changes may be applied to Atlas, its databases, the batch scheduler, the integration) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 228 Td (middleware, or the network paths Atlas depends on. Only emergency changes approved through the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 215 Td (Emergency Change Advisory Board \(ECAB\) are allowed. The day before the freeze \(BD-3\) is a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 202 Td (preparation day and changes already approved by CAB may still complete on that day, but must be) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 189 Td (finished before 18:00 UK time.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 167 Td (The month-end batch chain runs on the MEC_BATCH queue of the Atlas batch scheduler. The jobs) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 154 Td (run in the following fixed order, and each job must complete successfully and be reviewed) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 141 Td (before the next is released:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 119 Td (- ACCRUE: posts standard and recurring accruals for all entities.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 106 Td (- FXLOAD: loads European Central Bank reference exchange rates for period-end revaluation.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 93 Td (- ICRECON: reconciles intercompany balances across the four legal entities.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 80 Td (- GLRECON: runs the general ledger reconciliation and subledger tie-out.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 67 Td (- PAYX-MONTHLY: exports the monthly payroll file to Calderbrook Payroll.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 54 Td (- CLOSE-LOCK: locks the accounting period.) Tj ET
endstream
endobj
