stream
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 730 Td (BD+1 | 10:00 | GLRECON released | Atlas support engineer) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 718 Td (BD+1 | 14:00 | PAYX-MONTHLY host key check and release | Atlas support engineer, Payroll lead) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 706 Td (BD+2 | 09:15 | Stand-up; final adjustments | Close coordinator) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 694 Td (BD+3 | 09:15 | Stand-up; sign-off | Financial Controller) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 682 Td (BD+3 | After sign-off | CLOSE-LOCK; reports archived; window closes | Atlas support engineer) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 660 Td (A daily stand-up is held at 09:15 UK time on every day of the window in the Teams channel "MEC) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 647 Td (Bridge". The MEC Bridge channel is also the single place where job releases are announced and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 634 Td (approved. Approvals given verbally or in private chats are not valid for job release and must) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 621 Td (be restated in the channel.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 596 Td (6. Pre-close checks) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 574 Td (The following checks are completed on BD-3 and recorded in the close checklist attached to the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 561 Td (monthly Beacon close ticket \(category ATLAS-FIN, title "Month-end close YYYY-MM"\):) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 539 Td (- All CAB-approved changes affecting Atlas have completed and been closed in Beacon, or have) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 526 Td (   been deferred until after BD+3.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 513 Td (- No open SEV1 or SEV2 incidents affect Atlas or its integrations.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 500 Td (- The batch scheduler on atlas-batch-prd-01 is healthy and the MEC_BATCH queue has no jobs) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 487 Td (   left over from the previous month.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 474 Td (- The Calderbrook Payroll SFTP credentials in the Atlas credential vault have not expired.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 461 Td (- The previous month's close reports are present in the archive share on atlas-rpt-prd-01.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 448 Td (- The on-duty Atlas support engineer, DBA and service desk lead for each day of the window) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 435 Td (   are named in the close ticket.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 419 Td (7. Procedure) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 397 Td (Steps are numbered continuously across all phases. Do not skip a step. If a step cannot be) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 384 Td (completed, stop, record the reason in the close ticket and raise it in the MEC Bridge before) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 371 Td (continuing.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54 348 Td (Phase A: Preparation \(BD-3\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 326 Td (1. Confirm that the change freeze notice for the close window has been published to the IT) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 313 Td (   change calendar and the Atlas user community. The notice must state that only) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 300 Td (   ECAB-approved emergency changes are permitted between BD-2 and BD+3.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 287 Td (2. Check the health of the application tier. Confirm that atlas-app-prd-01 to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 274 Td (   atlas-app-prd-04 are all in service on the load balancer and that no node is showing) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 261 Td (   sustained CPU above 70% or heap usage above 85% in the monitoring dashboard.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 248 Td (3. Check replication from atlas-db-prd-01 to the standby atlas-db-prd-02.meridian.internal.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 235 Td (   Standby apply lag must be under 5 minutes. If lag is higher, involve the DBA before) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 222 Td (   continuing.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 209 Td (4. Check the archive log filesystem /u02/arch on atlas-db-prd-01. The warning threshold is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 196 Td (   80% used and the action threshold is 85% used. If usage is at or above 80% on BD-3, ask) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 183 Td (   the DBA to schedule an archive log purge before the backup, following the rule in step 18.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 170 Td (5. At 22:00 UK time on BD-3 the DBA starts the pre-close full backup of the Atlas production) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 157 Td (   database. The backup is tagged MEC-YYYYMM \(for example MEC-202505 for the May 2025 close\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 144 Td (   and is retained for 13 months. This retention overrides the standard 30-day daily) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 131 Td (   retention in the Backup and Retention Standard v2, so the DBA must apply the MEC retention) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 118 Td (   class explicitly when the job is submitted.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 105 Td (6. Before the window opens, confirm with the DBA that the MEC-YYYYMM backup completed) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 92 Td (   successfully and that a catalogue entry exists with the 13-month retention class. Record) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 79 Td (   the backup identifier in the close ticket.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54 65 Td (Phase B: Window opens \(BD-2\)) Tj ET
endstream
endobj
