12 0 obj
<< /Length 5290 >>
stream
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 729 Td (   Retrieve the current fingerprint presented by sftp.calderbrook-payroll.co.uk on port 2222) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 716 Td (   and compare it with the value recorded in the Atlas credential vault entry) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 703 Td (   payx/calderbrook/hostkey. If they differ, do not release the job; contact Calderbrook) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 690 Td (   Payroll through the bureau contact in the vault entry to confirm a legitimate key) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 677 Td (   rotation, update the vault entry only after confirmation, and record the change in the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 664 Td (   ATLAS-PAYX ticket. This step was added as action item AI-3 of postmortem INC-2025-007) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 651 Td (   \(Atlas payroll export failure, January 2025\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 638 Td (23. Confirm with the Payroll lead in the MEC Bridge that payroll data for the month is final) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 625 Td (   and that no further Keel changes affecting pay will be submitted for this cycle.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 612 Td (24. Test connectivity from atlas-batch-prd-01 to sftp.calderbrook-payroll.co.uk on port 2222) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 599 Td (   with atlasctl net check --host sftp.calderbrook-payroll.co.uk --port 2222. A failed check) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 586 Td (   usually means a firewall or proxy change and must be escalated to Network Operations) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 573 Td (   immediately, because the payroll bureau cut-off is 17:00 UK time on BD+1.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 560 Td (25. Release PAYX-MONTHLY with atlasctl job release PAYX-MONTHLY and monitor the transfer.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 547 Td (   Failure alerts for PAYX-MONTHLY are sent to the distribution list) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 534 Td (   atlas-oncall@meridian-instruments.com. The old list atlas-ops@meridian-instruments.com was) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 521 Td (   decommissioned and must not be used in any alert configuration.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 508 Td (26. Confirm receipt with Calderbrook Payroll. The bureau returns an acknowledgement file) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 495 Td (   within 30 minutes of a successful upload. Post the acknowledgement reference in the MEC) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 482 Td (   Bridge and attach it to the ATLAS-PAYX ticket.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54 468 Td (Phase E: Adjustments, sign-off and lock \(BD+2 to BD+3\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 446 Td (27. On BD+2, support Finance with late manual journals and reruns of individual reconciliation) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 433 Td (   reports. Reruns of whole batch jobs require the Financial Controller's approval in the MEC) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 420 Td (   Bridge.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 407 Td (28. On BD+3, obtain the Financial Controller's sign-off of the period in the MEC Bridge and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 394 Td (   record it in the close ticket.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 381 Td (29. Release CLOSE-LOCK with atlasctl job release CLOSE-LOCK. The job sets the configuration) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 368 Td (   key atlas.period.lock=true for the closed period in all four entities.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 355 Td (30. Verify the lock with atlasctl config get atlas.period.lock --period YYYY-MM and confirm) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 342 Td (   that a test posting into the closed period is rejected.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 329 Td (31. Generate the close report pack and archive it to the close archive share on) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 316 Td (   atlas-rpt-prd-01. Close reports are retained for 7 years.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 303 Td (32. Switch the "Finance reporting" data source back from atlas-db-prd-02.meridian.internal to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 290 Td (   the standard reporting configuration and confirm that a sample report runs.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 277 Td (33. Ask the service desk lead to return the Beacon category ATLAS-FIN to its normal default) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 264 Td (   priority.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 251 Td (34. Post the close summary in the MEC Bridge, close the stand-up series, and confirm to the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 238 Td (   change manager that the freeze for Atlas can be lifted at the end of BD+3.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 222 Td (8. Reopening a locked period) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 200 Td (A period locked by CLOSE-LOCK may only be reopened with the approval of the Financial) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 187 Td (Controller, recorded in Beacon as an ATLAS-FIN request with the approval attached. The Atlas) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 174 Td (support engineer then sets atlas.period.lock=false for the named entity and period only,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 161 Td (supports the correction, and sets the lock back to true on the same day. Reopening a period is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 148 Td (not a change under the Change Management Procedure, but every reopen is reported in the monthly) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 135 Td (Atlas service review.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 110 Td (9. Incident handling during the close) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 88 Td (Any issue that blocks the close calendar is declared a SEV2 incident according to the incident) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 75 Td (severity definitions \(it-incident-severity-definitions\). Examples include a failed batch job) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 62 Td (that cannot be rerun within two hours, loss of the standby replica, PAYX-MONTHLY failing after) Tj ET
endstream
endobj
